  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Voices Sudan (CVS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Voices Sudan (CVS), works towards improved two-way communication between people and service providers, including national and international actors. We will do this by continuous and consistent two-way communication with people affected by crisis, relay their concerns, questions and inputs with service providers and strengthen networks between national and international actors.   IEU will work towards two objectives: 1) Provide humanitarian stakeholders with data-driven, real-time community feedback and 2) Improve impact and sustainability of Accountability to Affected Populations (AAP) efforts by connecting local media, civil society and humanitarian actors, and specifically:  &#x2022;Conduct social media listening: Prioritising two-way communication channels people already use, data analysis focusing on sentiment and trust dynamics that could undermine service delivery and gaps in services and information about them to inform humanitarian decision-making and communication efforts.  &#x2022;In-person Listening Groups: Facilitated by a local partner, CVS will organise regular listening groups with key-parts of the affected population to understand their concerns, questions and criticism, identify information gaps and misinformation to tap into offline community conversations and inform humanitarian service providers with up-to-date community perspectives &#x2022;Round-tables: bring together national and international stakeholders, including local media to explore ways to strengthen each other&#x2019;s efforts, increase communication between service providers, local media and local service providers as a way to increase transparency and ultimately build trust.</narrative>
  </description>
